Keep the Lua program counter in a local instead of the CallInfo.

luaV_execute loaded and stored ci->u.l.savedpc on every instruction and
checked the hook mask for line hooks.  The pc now lives in a local and is
written back before calls, hooks, errors, metamethods and the collector
(Protect/savepc); hooks of any kind are checked at servicepoints only.
The opcode switch drops its range check, so load() and loadfile() accept
source text only (Lua 5.2 does not verify precompiled chunks).

